The headless application entrypoint: a debugger shell — session set, active
session, and each session's pane layout — for a host with no DOM.

This whole tree is a declared Embed SDK consumer, which is the directory-marker
spelling ci/test/sdk-facade-boundary.sh documents for exactly this case ("a
whole tree of consumer code — BlockTracer's debugger panes, a headless app
entrypoint — where marking each file would be noise").

Being a consumer is the point, not an accident of where the code landed.
BlockTracer.milestones.org M2a item 1 asks for a headless entrypoint and a
session/layout model that is not GoldenLayout-typed; building it strictly on
`codetracer_embed` is what turns "the facade is sufficient" from a claim into a
build failure when it stops being true. It is also what makes the outward half
of the boundary guard non-vacuous with something other than the SDK's own
conformance suite.
